The pairing and evaluation counts check out from the backend and loop code. The main statistical concern is the meta-D interval: the bootstrap resamples around observed family winners, while meta-D is bounded below by zero, so an interval above zero can overstate evidence against no true configuration interaction. I’m consolidating that with the documentation and integration findings now.
